hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3017","Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, narrated to us Jarir, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan (RA), who said:

""When the Prophet (ﷺ) conquered Makkah, I said, 'I will wear my clothes.'""

Also narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Kufi, narrated to us Ibn Fudayl, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman or Safwan ibn Abd al-Rahman (RA).

And narrated to us Abu Bishr al-Wasiti, narrated to us Khalid, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Safwan ibn Abd al-Rahman or Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan (RA), who said:

""The Prophet (ﷺ) arrived and entered the House (Ka'bah). I wore my clothes and set out. He (ﷺ) and his companions had exited the House, touching (the Black Stone) between the Hijr (Hatim) and the Black Stone (al-Hajar), placing their cheeks against the House.

When the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by the door, I entered between two men and asked, 'How did the Prophet (ﷺ) act?'

They said, 'He (ﷺ) prayed two rak'ahs at the place of the pillar opposite the House.'""

This is the narration of Ibn Fudayl.

**CHAPTER:**"
